Hi,

I've only done it for AlphaBIOS, and the floppy had just the files from 
the .zip with the firmware. I think it could be reduced to only 
LX164NT.ROM on a FAT formatted floppy.

Here are the SRM files for the 164LX (look for ALPHAPC164LX):

https://ia903105.us.archive.org/view_archive.php?archive=/12/items/alphasystemsfirmwareupdate60_agrcfbjbs/Alpha%20Systems%20Firmware%20Update%20v6.0%20%28AG-RCFBJ-BS%29%28Compaq%20Computer%20Corporation%29%28June%202001%29.iso

but I've never used SRM on my 164LX, so I can't tell you, which and how 
you should use. My guess is lx164srm.rom is the SRM ROM, lx164_v5_8.exe 
is definitely not an Windows .exe file (no MZ header), probably the 
"loadable firmware upgrade" executable, that should be renamed to 
fwupdate.exe and put on the floppy. Not sure what the .sys files are.

I would try with lx164srm.rom first, then try fwupdate.exe.

--
Regards,
Piotr Gliźniewicz


