Hi,

I have successfully fail-safe boot on the PC164SX(not PC164LX but very =
similar) in the following way:

1.set CF1 to OFF at power down
2.copy an SRM exe file renamed to "fwupdate.exe" from "sx164_v5_8.exe", =
for example, to FAT formatted FD
3.insert the FD and power on. It sounds "1-2-3" BEEP
4.if sx164_v5_8.exe, because no "option firmware", eject the FD and =
press return
5.Now, update program starts
6.use "list" command to display a target SRM
7.use "update" command to update to target SRM
8.(optional)use "verify" command to verify update
9.power off
10.set CF1 to ON
11.power on

ftp.hp.com is probably official, but not announced, site. It seems to =
DEC's gatekeeper site. For AlphaPC164LX, visit =
/pub/alphaserver/firmware/retired_platforms/alphapc/alphapc164lx/.

--=20
Yoshihiko Iwama

